# Git and release

`main` is protected. Work on `feature/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` branches. Commit only when the user or release workflow asked for a commit.

Commit messages state intent. Avoid "update files", "misc", and "fix stuff". Do not require Conventional Commits unless this repository later adopts them.

The release path is verify, then release engineer, then commit, push the feature branch, pull request, CI, and human merge. Verification evidence comes before the pull request.

Agents may push non-protected branches and open pull requests. Agents do not merge `main`, force-push, skip hooks, rewrite shared history, or publish a release without explicit human approval.

Pull request text uses `.github/pull_request_template.md` and drops sections that do not apply.
